WEBVTT

NOTE On-screen visual text only; this approved video has no audio track.

1
00:00:00.500 --> 00:00:07.350
One encoder transforms the image and another transforms the text query.

2
00:00:07.350 --> 00:00:14.200
Their comparable representations allow candidates to be ordered by similarity.

3
00:00:14.200 --> 00:00:21.867
The system returns a record; writing an answer requires a separate generative stage.

4
00:00:22.367 --> 00:00:29.217
The visual encoder emits a three-component vector in this example.

5
00:00:29.217 --> 00:00:36.067
A learned matrix projects it into four components accepted by the receiving model.

6
00:00:36.067 --> 00:00:43.417
Changing dimensions connects interfaces but does not guarantee that all visual evidence survives.

7
00:00:43.917 --> 00:00:50.767
The text query asks about the object on the right.

8
00:00:50.767 --> 00:00:57.617
Attention weights visual regions and combines their representations.

9
00:00:57.617 --> 00:01:06.417
Selection depends on the query; an attention map alone does not establish a causal explanation.

10
00:01:06.917 --> 00:01:13.767
The input interleaves a first image with its caption and then a second image.

11
00:01:13.767 --> 00:01:20.933
The question refers to the second image, not an unordered mixture of both.

12
00:01:20.933 --> 00:01:28.283
Keeping modality boundaries and positions preserves which evidence accompanies each fragment.

13
00:01:28.783 --> 00:01:35.633
Four visual regions contain information, including a small label in the fourth.

14
00:01:35.633 --> 00:01:42.483
A two-representation summary merges or discards some detail.

15
00:01:42.483 --> 00:01:50.150
Fewer tokens can reduce work, but the small label must still be tested for recoverability.

16
00:01:50.650 --> 00:01:57.500
A system can produce text and audio chunks at different rates.

17
00:01:57.500 --> 00:02:04.350
Identifiers and boundaries associate each chunk with the correct content.

18
00:02:04.350 --> 00:02:12.767
Coordination belongs to the system: multiple modalities do not prove the entire path is full duplex.

